  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a N×MN \\times MN×M matrix AAA, filled with **distinct** numbers. You can start at any cell. If you are currently at cell (x1,y1)(x_1, y_1)(x1​,y1​), then you can jump to any other cell (x2,y2)(x_2, y_2)(x2​,y2​), if and only if the following two conditions are satisfied:\n\n\n\nAx2,y2&gt;Ax1,y1A_{x_2, y_2} \\gt A_{x_1, y_1}Ax2​,y2​​&gt;Ax1​,y1​​\n\n\n\n\nManhattan distance between Ax2,y2A_{x_2, y_2}Ax2​,y2​​ and Ax1,y1A_{x_1, y_1}Ax1​,y1​​ &gt;S \\gt S&gt;S. Formally, ∣x1−x2∣+∣y1−y2∣&gt;S|x_1 - x_2| + |y_1 - y_2| \\gt S∣x1​−x2​∣+∣y1​−y2​∣&gt;S.\n\n\n\nLet VVV be the set of the cells visited by you.\n\nMaximize the value of ∑(x,y)∈V&nbsp;Ax,y\\sum_{(x, y) \\in V} \\text{ }A_{x, y}∑(x,y)∈V​&nbsp;Ax,y​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains the number TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains three integers N,M,SN, M, SN,M,S - the parameters defined in the statement.\nThen NNN lines follow, with MMM integers in each line.\nEach of the next NNN lines contains MMM integers, where the jjj-th integer in iii-th line is equal to Ai,jA_{i, j}Ai,j​\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase output the maximum possible value of ∑(x,y)∈V&nbsp;Ax,y\\sum_{(x, y) \\in V} \\text{ }A_{x, y}∑(x,y)∈V​&nbsp;Ax,y​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,M≤10001 \\le N, M \\le 10001≤N,M≤1000",
      "0≤S≤N+M−20 \\le S \\le N + M - 20≤S≤N+M−2.",
      "1≤Ai,j≤1091 \\le A_{i, j} \\le 10^91≤Ai,j​≤109.",
      "It's guaranteed that all Ai,jA_{i, j}Ai,j​ are distinct.",
      "It's guaranteed that sum of N×MN \\times MN×M over all test cases doesn't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
