      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 2 2\n1 2\n4 5\n7 8\n2 2 0\n100 99\n98 97",
        "output": "9\n394",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case-1: It is optimal start at cell (1,1)(1, 1)(1,1), then jump to cell (3,2)(3, 2)(3,2). Therefore answer is A1,1+A3,2=1+8=9A_{1, 1} + A_{3, 2} = 1 + 8 = 9A1,1​+A3,2​=1+8=9.\nTest case-2: It is optimal to start at (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2) and follow this path: (2,2)→(2,1)→(1,2)→(1,1)(2, 2) \\rightarrow (2, 1) \\rightarrow (1, 2) \\rightarrow (1, 1)(2,2)→(2,1)→(1,2)→(1,1). Therefore answer is the sum of all the four cells =394= 394=394."
      }
